{
 "about": "Settings' sidebar navigated with the arrows as ONE list, as a Mac's System Settings sidebar (docs/adr/0039-keyboard-access.mdx; Bloom's SettingsLayout rail): Settings with the shell, the screen reader on in Spanish. Tab lands on the sidebar once, on its selected row; ↓ ↑, End and Home select the rows and show their panes, the keyboard following the selection and each row said once, selected; ↓ at the end goes nowhere; Tab goes on to the pane's first control and Shift+Tab back to the selected row. The sidebar is one list of its rows, its groups apart by space alone (no headings, as a Mac’s); its search field is the first stop. Every step checks the keyboard's focus, what the assistive technology holds, what the reader says and what is announced. At 1 (1280 × 720).",
 "locale": "es_ES.UTF-8",
 "module": "OxyOSSettings",
 "window": [
  900,
  640
 ],
 "shell": "OxyOSShell",
 "app": {
  "id": "so.oxy.settings",
  "title": "Settings"
 },
 "settings": {
  "app": "so.oxy.settings",
  "preferences": {
   "appearance": "light",
   "accent": "oxy"
  }
 },
 "reader": {},
 "steps": [
  {
   "name": "Settings' window with the shell, the reader on, nothing of it focused",
   "do": [
    "wait",
    1500
   ],
   "allow_unchanged": true,
   "expect": {
    "keyboard_focus": null,
    "spoken": [],
    "announcements": []
   }
  },
  {
   "name": "Tab: the sidebar's search field first, as a Mac's System Settings has it at the sidebar's top, said once",
   "do": [
    "key",
    [
     15
    ]
   ],
   "allow_unchanged": true,
   "expect": {
    "react": {
     "focus@settings-search": 1,
     "selectionChange@settings-search": 1
    },
    "keyboard_focus": {
     "target": "settings-search",
     "ring": true
    },
    "spoken": [
     {
      "text": "Buscar en Ajustes, campo de búsqueda",
      "interrupting": true
     }
    ],
    "announcements": []
   }
  },
  {
   "name": "Tab again: the keyboard on the sidebar's selected row, Appearance, said once with its state; the sidebar is one list of its rows, its groups apart with no headings, as a Mac’s",
